Downloads extensions and spellcheck dictionaries directly from Google.

Helium fetches these through its own proxy (Helium services), which Rooster
keeps off, so with this patch they go where Chrome gets them:
- extension installs and updates: clients2.google.com (Chrome Web Store)
- Web Store item details for installs: chromewebstore.googleapis.com
- spellcheck dictionaries: redirector.gvt1.com
Google sees the request (and the extension IDs being installed or updated),
as it would in Chrome. Extension usage pings stay off (see
no-helium-endpoints.patch). helium_services_helpers.cc isn't on the domain
substitution list, so these URLs survive the build.

--- a/components/helium_services/helium_services_helpers.cc
+++ b/components/helium_services/helium_services_helpers.cc
@@ -81,13 +81,11 @@
 }
 
 bool ShouldAccessExtensionService(const PrefService& prefs) {
-    return ShouldAccessServices(prefs) &&
-            prefs.GetBoolean(prefs::kHeliumExtProxyEnabled);
+    return true;
 }
 
 bool ShouldAccessDictionaryService(const PrefService& prefs) {
-    return ShouldAccessServices(prefs) &&
-            prefs.GetBoolean(prefs::kHeliumSpellcheckEnabled);
+    return true;
 }
 
 bool ShouldFetchBangs(const PrefService& prefs) {
@@ -101,28 +99,17 @@
 }
 
 GURL GetExtensionUpdateURL(const PrefService& prefs) {
-    if (!ShouldAccessExtensionService(prefs)) {
-        return GetDummyURL();
-    }
-
-    return GetServicesBaseURL(prefs).Resolve("/ext");
+    return GURL("https://clients2.google.com/service/update2/crx");
 }
 
